{
  "company_name": "FabSight Analytics",
  "industry": "Semiconductor",
  "use_case": "Virtual metrology and inline defect detection for wafer fabrication",
  "space_title": "FabSight - Virtual Metrology & Defect Detection 🔬",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Semiconductor\n\n**Use case:** Virtual Metrology & Inline Defect Detection\n\nFabSight Analytics — inline metrology and defect-inspection analytics across 20 process recipes spanning litho, etch, CMP, deposition, and implant. Process Engineering and Equipment Engineering use this space to monitor critical-dimension and overlay drift, validate virtual-metrology model accuracy versus physical measurements, and target kill-defect hotspots; the Director of Yield uses it to size sampling cost reduction and pull-ahead opportunities from in-situ predictions.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Critical dimension (cd_nm) — mean wafer CD; advanced-node targets tight control, e.g. 3nm gate CD ~20 nm with <1.5% within-wafer variation\n- Overlay error (nm) — layer-to-layer alignment; 3nm/5nm nodes require <2 nm\n- Film thickness deviation (nm) — process drift signal; spec typically ±5%\n- Virtual metrology prediction error % — actual vs predicted; target <3% MAPE\n- Defect density per cm² — fab-wide defectivity; mature <0.10, ramping <0.30\n- Kill ratio % — share of defects that cause die failure; lower kill-ratio = healthier defect mix\n- Out-of-spec measurement count — excursion driver for process holds\n- Wafers inspected per month — sampling coverage; ML inspection enables 100% virtual coverage\n\n**Data sources**\n- `wafer_measurements` — daily metrology measurements with CD, overlay, and thickness readings\n- `metrology_predictions` — weekly VM prediction batches with model accuracy and confidence scores\n- `defect_detections` — monthly defect-type summaries with kill ratio and inspection coverage",
  "schema_basename": "semiconductor_virtual_metrology",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "wafer_measurements",
      "description": "Daily wafer measurement records from inline metrology tools capturing thickness, CD, overlay, and film stress across process steps.",
      "columns": [
        {
          "name": "measurement_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Unique wafer measurement identifier",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CONCAT('WM-', LPAD(CAST({id_seq} AS STRING), 5, '0'))"
        },
        {
          "name": "measurement_date",
          "sql_type": "DATE",
          "comment": "Date the measurement was taken",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "dt"
        },
        {
          "name": "recipe_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Process recipe identifier",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "recipe_name",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Human-readable recipe name",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "process_step",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Process step category",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "tool_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Metrology tool identifier",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CASE WHEN {status_noise} < 0.20 THEN 'MET-ASML-01' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.40 THEN 'MET-KLA-02' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.55 THEN 'MET-AMAT-03' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.70 THEN 'MET-HITC-04' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.85 THEN 'MET-NOVA-05' ELSE 'MET-ONTO-06' END"
        },
        {
          "name": "thickness_nm",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Film thickness measurement in nanometers",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(GREATEST(1.0, 50.0 + ({qty_noise} - 0.5) * 40.0), 2)"
        },
        {
          "name": "cd_nm",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Critical dimension measurement in nanometers",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(GREATEST(2.0, 20.0 + ({qty_noise} - 0.5) * 15.0), 2)"
        },
        {
          "name": "overlay_nm",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Overlay alignment error in nanometers",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(GREATEST(0.1, 3.0 + ({qty_noise} - 0.5) * 4.0), 3)"
        },
        {
          "name": "measurement_status",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Measurement result status",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CASE WHEN {alt_status_noise} < 0.70 THEN 'In Spec' WHEN {alt_status_noise} < 0.88 THEN 'Warning' ELSE 'Out of Spec' END"
        }
      ],
