  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Virtual Metrology (VM) and inline defect detection for a wafer fab running 20 process recipes across litho, etch, CMP, deposition, and implant steps. Stakeholders include Process Engineering (CD/overlay/thickness control), Yield Engineering (defect density, kill ratio), and Equipment Engineering (tool-to-tool variation). Virtual metrology models predict wafer measurements from in-situ sensor traces, enabling 100% virtual sampling versus 5–10% physical sampling.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Critical dimension = cd_nm (mean nm per measurement; no separate within-wafer uniformity column)\n- Overlay error = overlay_nm; 3nm/5nm target <2 nm, mature nodes <5 nm\n- Film thickness = thickness_nm; spec usually ±5% of target\n- VM prediction error = prediction_error_pct; healthy model <3% MAPE\n- VM confidence = confidence_score (0–1); flag predictions <0.7 for physical re-measurement\n- Defect density = defect_density_per_cm2; mature <0.10, ramping <0.30\n- Kill ratio = kill_ratio_pct; lower is better (fewer yield-killing defects in the mix)\n- Out-of-spec count = measurement_status indicates 'Out-of-Spec'; excursion trigger\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - wafer_measurement_metrics (source: wafer_measurements) — dims: measurement_date, process_step, tool_id, measurement_status; measures: total_measurements, avg_thickness_nm, avg_cd_nm, avg_overlay_nm, out_of_spec_count, unique_recipe_count, max_thickness_nm.\n  - defect_detection_metrics (source: defect_detections) — dims: detection_month, process_step, defect_type; measures: avg_defect_density, avg_kill_ratio_pct, total_wafers_inspected, total_defects_found, unique_recipe_count, max_defect_density_per_cm2.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. recipe_id, recipe_name, predicted_thickness_nm, actual_thickness_nm, prediction_error_pct, confidence_score, model_version).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Which 10 process recipes have the highest average defect density in the trailing 12 months?",
    "Show monthly out-of-spec measurement count by process step for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which defect types are driving the highest kill ratios this quarter — what are we losing yield to?",
    "Rank metrology tools by average overlay error — which of the 6 tools need re-qualification?",
    "How has average VM prediction error trended monthly — is the model drifting?",
    "Which process steps have the highest standard deviation of cd_nm across recent measurements, and which tools are driving the spread?",
    "What is the total wafers inspected by process step in the trailing 6 months — where is sampling coverage lowest?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique recipes?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT measurement_date, MEASURE(unique_recipe_count) AS unique_recipe_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.wafer_measurement_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY measurement_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest thickness nm changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT measurement_date, MEASURE(max_thickness_nm) AS max_thickness_nm",
        "FROM {fqn}.wafer_measurement_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY measurement_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total defects found changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT detection_month, MEASURE(total_defects_found) AS total_defects_found",
        "FROM {fqn}.defect_detection_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY detection_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total film thickness measurement in nanometers break down by process recipe identifier for 'In Spec' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT recipe_id, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(thickness_nm) AS total_thickness_nm",
        "FROM {fqn}.wafer_measurements",
        "WHERE measurement_status = 'In Spec' GROUP BY recipe_id ORDER BY total_thickness_nm DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total model-predicted film thickness in nm over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(predicted_thickness_nm) AS total_predicted_thickness_nm",
        "FROM {fqn}.metrology_predictions",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average estimated percentage of defects that are yield-killing changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT detection_month, AVG(kill_ratio_pct) AS avg_kill_ratio_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.defect_detections",
        "GROUP BY detection_month ORDER BY detection_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has out of spec count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT measurement_date, MEASURE(out_of_spec_count) AS out_of_spec_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.wafer_measurement_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY measurement_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
